course: dictionary
lesson: 7657
title: Animal words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word like pronghorn names one kind of thing. Read the sentence around it to find out what kind. «The pronghorn, a deer-like animal of North American grasslands, can run fast for a long time.» The words a deer-like animal tell you what it is, and grasslands tell you where it lives.
explain: Some sentences compare two things to help you. «Horns, like those of cows and goats, have a bone core covered with keratin and stay for life; the pronghorn of America sheds the outer cover of its horns every year, a bit of both.» The sentence first says the horns are like cows' and goats' horns, then shows how the pronghorn's are different.
explain: Check a new word by swapping in your meaning. Try «The pronghorn is a deer-like animal of the grasslands» and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have understood it.
fact: A pronghorn is a deer-like animal of the grasslands of North America.
fact: The name «pronghorn» comes from its forked horns, which are pronged, or split into points.
fact: The pronghorn is the fastest land animal in America.
fact: A pronghorn can run about 90 km/h (55 mph) and keep going much longer than a cheetah.
fact: Many people wrongly call the pronghorn an antelope, so check a dictionary if you are not sure.
exercise: «The pronghorn, a deer-like animal of North American grasslands, can run fast.» What is a pronghorn? | A kind of cow | A fish found in rivers | A bird that cannot fly | *A deer-like animal of the grasslands of North America
exercise: Why is it called a pronghorn? | It lives in the sea | *It has forked, pronged horns | It has a long, thin neck | It sleeps all day in the trees
exercise: Many people wrongly call the pronghorn something else. What do they wrongly call it? | A cheetah | A cow | A goat | *An antelope
test: The pronghorn is the fastest land animal in which place? | Africa | *America | Europe | Asia
test: What does the pronghorn shed every year? | Its fur | *The outer cover of its horns | Its bones | Its teeth
exam: The pronghorn is the fastest land animal in America. What does fastest mean? | Tallest | Quietest | *Quickest
